  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Clear Drawers",
    "overview": "Every place is a frosted drawer you can see into, and a location path is the stack of drawers. The ground is pale sea-glass, cool and quiet. Colour belongs to rooms: each room carries one of six soft tints. One accent is the only loud colour: deep teal by default, or whichever of seven the user picks in Settings. It marks the one main action on each screen. The category default is a grey list with the path as a faint subtitle. This system turns that path into the picture itself: a short stack of same-height tabs hanging from one thin spine.\n\nThe world is Material 3 tuned rather than replaced. Scheme roles, shapes, motion and navigation come from the platform. Character comes from the palette, from drawer geometry repeated at every scale (list row, place header, app icon), and from a refusal to add boxes. Hierarchy comes from Material type size and weight in the device's own sans, so the app follows the user's font and font-size settings. Cards and dividers are not used for hierarchy. The density is calm: one item per row, generous 16dp gutters, and enough room under the list for the extended FAB.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Frosted sea-glass ground (light and dark), with tonal surface containers for depth and no card shadows.",
      "The accent (deep teal by default) on exactly one main action per screen. Secondary actions are tonal or outlined.",
      "Six room tints (seafoam, amber, rose, lavender, sky, sage). Each is a light/dark tonal pair, picked by a hash of the room name.",
      "The drawer path is the signature: one spine, fixed 22dp tabs, a tinted room tab, and white slip-label inner tabs.",
      "The device's system sans at stock Material roles. No bundled font.",
      "Two motions only: a shared-axis Y \"drawer pull\" into and out of places, and a fade-through everywhere else."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "Each screen has at most one deep-teal action: the FAB on a list, the filled confirm in a sheet. Everything else is tonal (`mist-tonal`), outlined, or a text button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Room Owns Its Colour Rule",
        "body": "Tints identify rooms and never encode status or emphasis. An item's avatar, its room tab and its room's swatch always share one tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Own Palette Rule",
        "body": "Dynamic (wallpaper) colour is deliberately off. The palette is the app's identity, and a room's tint has to stay stable from one launch to the next.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Borrowed Voice Rule",
        "body": "Never bundle a font or hard-code sp sizes outside the Material roles. Every text style is a `MaterialTheme.typography` role.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Section titles are sentence case at title-small in muted ink. Never use uppercase tracking labels above them.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Frosted, Not Lifted Rule",
        "body": "To show that something sits on top, use the next surface-container step or a hairline. Don't add shadows to custom surfaces.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give each screen exactly one deep-teal action: the extended FAB on lists, the filled confirm in sheets.",
      "Do use tonal (mist) for secondary actions and outlined for cancel or alternative choices.",
      "Do show every location as a Drawer Path: one 2dp spine, 22dp tabs, a 10dp indent per level (at most three steps), and the room tab tinted while inner tabs are slips.",
      "Do show paths relative to the current place when listing inside a room or box.",
      "Do pair every room tint with its own ink (`on-room-*`), in both light and dark.",
      "Do keep 16dp gutters and 96dp bottom clearance on any list with an extended FAB.",
      "Do use the 300ms shared-axis Y only for moving into or out of a place, and fade-through for everything else.",
      "Do use Material type roles only, so the user's font and size settings carry through."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn on dynamic (wallpaper) colour. The palette and stable room tints are the identity.",
      "Don't use deep teal for decoration, selection, or a second action on the same screen.",
      "Don't vary drawer tab height or text size to show depth. Depth is the indent, and the tab scale is fixed so paths compare at a glance.",
      "Don't use room tints for status or emphasis. A tint means \"this room\".",
      "Don't wrap rows in cards or add shadows to custom surfaces. Depth is tonal.",
      "Don't add uppercase tracked labels above section titles. Titles are sentence-case title-small.",
      "Don't treat two rooms that share a tint as related. Six tints chosen by name hash can collide, and that is a known limit, not a meaning."
    ]
  }
}
